      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): support GPT-5.6 Sol Pro effort",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- treat GPT-5.6 Sol version selection and the independent Pro effort control as separate browser state\n- add explicit `--browser-thinking-time pro` support with exact-label, fail-closed verification\n- reject explicit `pro` before browser submission unless GPT-5.6 Sol is selected with model strategy `select`\n- update CLI, config, consult MCP, image MCP, docs, the bundled Oracle skill, and focused regression coverage\n\n## Reproduction\n\nOn current `main`, this failed after the UI showed GPT-5.6 Sol with Pro selected:\n\n```text\nUnable to find model option matching \"GPT-5.6 Sol\"... Available: ... Pro, GPT-5.6 Sol.\n```\n\nThe picker now verifies the Sol version independently from the Pro effort pill, but only when Pro was explicitly requested. A carried-over Pro pill remains incompatible with base Sol.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm check`\n- `pnpm vitest run` — 144 files passed, 18 skipped; 1,567 tests passed, 43 skipped\n- focused CLI, config, browser, consult MCP, and image MCP regressions — 233 passed\n- `pnpm build`\n- live Chrome smoke test with `--model gpt-5.6-sol --browser-thinking-time pro`\n  - `Thinking time: Pro (already selected)`\n  - `requested=GPT-5.6 Sol; resolved=GPT-5.6 Sol; verified=yes`\n  - exact response marker: `SOL PRO REVIEW SMOKE OK`\n- guarded non-Sol CLI smoke with `--model gpt-5.4 --browser-thinking-time pro`\n  - exited 1 before browser acquisition\n  - `Browser thinking time \"pro\" requires GPT-5.6 Sol with model strategy \"select\".`\n- Oracle GPT-5.6 Sol + Pro code review: `BLOCKERS None`, `VERDICT APPROVE`\n\nThis is a focused picker/effort compatibility fix and does not attempt the broader model-inventory redesign discussed in #319.",
